From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:29:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/win32: upscaling and frame generation in the composed
 present

Off by default.  With MESA_WSI_ENHANCE_SCALER / MESA_WSI_ENHANCE_FG or
the HKLM\SOFTWARE\Helios Enhance* values (a per-exe profile under
HKLM\SOFTWARE\Helios\Enhance\<exe>), a composed swapchain's DXGI flip swap
chain is the window's size and every present runs compute passes on the
application's queue (wsi_swapchain::present_cmd, submitted after the
application's semaphores and before the present's fence):

  scale    FSR 1 (EASU, then RCAS with the sharpness), bicubic,
           bilinear, nearest or integer, into the picture region of an
           output slot (a D3D11 shared texture of the window's size),
           aspect kept with black bars or stretched
  framegen 2x, 3x, 4x or adaptive (fill to the refresh or a target fps):
           a luma pyramid of the frame, block-matching optical flow
           between the last two frames, coarse to fine and symmetric
           about the generated moment, and each generated picture
           interpolated at output resolution into its own slot

The present thread waits for the passes, hands the application's image
back at once and presents the slots, generated ones first, paced a frame
interval apart (a high-resolution timer); a newer frame cuts a cycle short.
The application's thread never waits for a picture's time.  Generation
steps aside after a pause, when the frame rate is near the refresh, and
with low latency when the game reaches the target itself.

With a scaler the surface reports no current extent, so DXVK, vkd3d-proton
and native applications that take the swapchain size from the swapchain
render at their own resolution.  Settings changes that need new buffers
return VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR.  Statistics every 5 s in helios-wsi-<pid>.log
(pictures shown, GPU time per pass from timestamps), per frame in
enhance-<pid>-*.csv with MESA_WSI_ENHANCE_STATS=1.

Passes: GLSL compute compiled to SPIR-V by glslangValidator at build time
(src/vulkan/wsi/enhance), push descriptors and push constants.
